00:01:30.858 --> 00:01:34.039
The monks of Serra are rebuilding their
main debating hall.

00:01:36.444 --> 00:01:41.567
Serra was originally the second largest
monastery in Tibet, where more than 6,000

00:01:41.607 --> 00:01:43.048
monks studied and lived.

00:01:50.392 --> 00:01:54.014
Each morning, the monks gather for the
early morning debate session.

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:06.791
In the monastic universities, the monks
study the classical Buddhist subjects.

00:02:07.592 --> 00:02:12.693
These subjects include logic and
epistemology, psychology, philosophy,

00:02:13.134 --> 00:02:14.494
cosmology and ethics,

00:02:14.994 --> 00:02:17.715
as well as Buddhist meditational theory
and practice.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:25.744
Traditionally, the monks refine their
scholarly knowledge through debate, both

00:02:25.784 --> 00:02:28.046
in the morning session as now, and

00:02:28.086 --> 00:02:29.187
again each evening.

00:02:37.154 --> 00:02:40.937
The theme being debated here is the
question of what constitutes a particular

00:02:41.057 --> 00:02:43.419
act as being virtuous or non-virtuous.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:49.965
Is an act virtuous or non-virtuous due to
the motivation, the act itself, or the

00:02:50.005 --> 00:02:50.705
consequence?

00:02:51.527 --> 00:02:55.651
Also, what is the relationship between the
degree of the individual's knowledge or

00:02:55.751 --> 00:02:57.813
ignorance, as the act occurs,

00:02:58.474 --> 00:03:01.136
and the individual's responsibility for
their actions?

