00:09:38.499 --> 00:09:43.541
In Tibetan society, knowledge is handed
down from generation to generation, from

00:09:43.601 --> 00:09:44.601
master to student,

00:09:45.122 --> 00:09:49.223
primarily through the giving of oral
commentarial explanations to the key

00:09:49.303 --> 00:09:50.264
classical texts.

00:09:51.584 --> 00:09:56.306
These oral lineages have mainly remained
unbroken from as long ago as the time of

00:09:56.307 --> 00:09:58.327
the Buddha himself in the 5th century

00:09:58.427 --> 00:09:59.127
BC.

00:10:00.132 --> 00:10:04.894
The Dalai Lama has received many of these
oral lineages from his teachers and today

00:10:05.014 --> 00:10:06.415
he is beginning the 12-day

00:10:06.515 --> 00:10:11.598
explication of a major text known as The
Lamb Illuminating the Five Stages.

00:10:12.658 --> 00:10:16.640
This text is a guide to the advanced
levels of deep meditative states.

00:10:21.202 --> 00:10:24.324
Before the teaching begins, the monks
recite the Heart Sutra.

00:10:24.924 --> 00:10:28.265
which is a quintessence of the Buddha
Shakyamuni's teaching on the way of

00:10:28.305 --> 00:10:30.726
realizing the ultimate nature of mind and
phenomena.

00:10:32.146 --> 00:10:36.368
Recognizing that our mental and sensory
processes condition all our perceptions

00:10:36.948 --> 00:10:38.989
and that ultimately all phenomena are

00:10:39.069 --> 00:10:44.090
empty of inherent existence leads to the
realization that the mind's actual nature

00:10:44.150 --> 00:10:45.991
is a pure mirror-like awareness,

00:10:46.711 --> 00:10:49.152
a blissful union of emptiness and form.

00:10:53.208 --> 00:10:57.594
